md`# brain-feedback

Feedback about the Brain's page, written on the page. A note placed with \`@tomlarkworthy/annotate\` is filed as a \`feedback\` issue of \`brain-issues\`, and from then on the note shows that issue.

| | |
|---|---|
| Where | The Brain's own address, with the owner signed in. Not a portal, not a page opened with \`#verify=\`, not a file. \`feedbackOn\` says which. |
| Start one | The page menu, Annotate, Feedback; or select text and press the chip \`feedback\`. Click what the note is about, write, press **File**. |
| What is filed | \`issue.open\` with kind \`feedback\`, the label \`annotation\`, the id \`fb-<note id>\`, the first line as the title, and \`about\` the Worker whose module was clicked (\`brain\` when it is none). The body is the text, one sentence that says where, and the anchor as JSON in a fence named \`annotation\`. |
| On page load | \`issue.list?label=annotation\`, then \`issue.get\` for each, and a note is placed for each at its anchor. Asked again every 30 s while the tab is visible; an issue is read again only when its \`updated_at\` moved. |
| Progress | The note shows the state, what the issue is part of or linked to, and the last comment, move or review with who wrote it. |
| Done | When the issue is closed the note reads **Done** with the reason, and has **Remove**. |
| Remove | On a closed issue, Remove (or the note's own ×) takes the label \`annotation\` off with \`issue.label\`, so no page loads the note again. The issue stays in the record. On an open issue the × hides the note until the page is loaded again. A note not yet filed is deleted. |

No Worker and no table: the record is the issue. The label is the switch, so anyone who may label can take a note off every page; the loop's briefs say not to.

The cells of a note are kept in this module (\`home\` of the kind), not in the module the note points at. A note on a Worker's panel is then not part of that Worker's source when the page exports it.

A note's box can be moved; the new place is not kept. Text typed and not filed is lost on a reload.
`
// %%
// The Brain's own page, the owner signed in. A verify page runs a Worker's tests and is left alone.
feedbackOn = !!brainOrigin && !brainPortal && !!(brainWho && brainWho.owner) && !/[#&]verify=/.test(location.hash)
// %%
feedbackLimits = ({ title: 120, text: 4000, shown: 400, everyMs: 30000, label: "annotation", kind: "feedback", home: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-feedback", fence: "`".repeat(3) + "annotation\n", says: "Annotated on the Brain's page: " })
// %%
// One sentence a reader of the issue can act on without the page.
// near: the text of the element under the note's tip, for a note that marks no text of its own.
feedbackWhere = (anchor = {}, near = "") =>
  feedbackLimits.says +
  [anchor.module && `module \`${anchor.module}\``, anchor.cell && `cell \`${anchor.cell}\``, anchor.quote && anchor.quote.exact ? `at the text "${String(anchor.quote.exact).slice(0, 200)}"` : near && `on the element that reads "${String(near).replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim().slice(0, 120)}"`].filter(Boolean).concat(anchor.module || anchor.cell ? [] : ["no cell"]).join(", ") + "."
// %%
feedbackBody = (text, where, near = "") => `${String(text).trim()}\n\n${feedbackWhere(where.anchor, near)}\n\n${feedbackLimits.fence}${JSON.stringify(where)}\n${"`".repeat(3)}`
// %%
// { text, anchor, box } of a body feedbackBody wrote, or null.
feedbackParse = (body) => {
  const s = String(body || ""), at = s.lastIndexOf(feedbackLimits.fence);
  if (at < 0) return null;
  const from = at + feedbackLimits.fence.length, end = s.indexOf("\n" + "`".repeat(3), from);
  try {
    const where = JSON.parse(s.slice(from, end < 0 ? undefined : end));
    if (!where || typeof where.anchor !== "object" || !where.anchor) return null;
    const head = s.slice(0, at), said = head.lastIndexOf("\n\n" + feedbackLimits.says);
    return { text: (said < 0 ? head : head.slice(0, said)).trim(), anchor: where.anchor, box: where.box || null };
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
// %%
// What a note shows of an issue's events: the last one that says something, and the reason it was closed with.
feedbackProgress = (ticket) => {
  const { issue, events = [] } = ticket;
  const who = (by = {}) => (String(by.holder || "").startsWith("secret:") ? by.holder.slice(7).replace(/^issues-/, "") : by.caller || "");
  const said = (e) => e.body || e.reason || (e.type === "linked" ? `${e.remove ? "no longer " : ""}${e.rel}${e.to ? " " + e.to : ""}` : e.type === "swapped" ? "moved to another workflow" : "");
  const last = [...events].reverse().find((e) => e.type !== "opened" && said(e));
  const closing = [...events].reverse().find((e) => e.type === "moved" && e.to === issue.state);
  const links = [issue.parent && `part of ${issue.parent}`, ...(issue.links || []).map((l) => `${l.rel} ${l.to}`)].filter(Boolean);
  return { state: issue.state, closed: !!issue.closed, links, reason: issue.closed && closing ? closing.reason || "" : "", last: last ? { who: who(last.by), at: last.at, type: last.type, text: said(last) } : null };
}
// %%
// The notes of one page. client: issue.* calls. store: annotate's (create, remove, patch, get, all, refresh).
feedbackApp = ({ client, store, about = () => "brain", near = () => "", limits = feedbackLimits }) => {
  // tickets: issue id to what issue.get answered. of: note id to issue id. hidden: open issues whose note was closed here.
  const tickets = new Map(), of = new Map(), els = new Map(), drafts = new Map(), says = new Map(), hidden = new Set(), filing = new Set();
  let busy = false;
  for (const a of store.all()) if (a.kind === limits.kind && a.issue) of.set(a.id, a.issue);
  const get = async (iss) => {
    const r = await client.query("issue.get", { id: iss });
    tickets.set(iss, r);
    return r;
  };
  const cut = (s, n) => (String(s).length > n ? String(s).slice(0, n) + "…" : String(s));
  const has = async (id) => (await store.refresh(), !!store.get(id));
  const view = (id) => {
    const iss = of.get(id), t = iss && tickets.get(iss), muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
    if (!iss) {
      const box = htl.html`<textarea rows="4" maxlength=${limits.text} placeholder="What is wrong or wanted here" style="font:inherit;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box">${drafts.get(id) || ""}</textarea>`;
      box.oninput = () => drafts.set(id, box.value);
      return htl.html`<div data-feedback="draft">${box}<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => file(id)}>File</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || "Filed as a feedback issue."}</span></div></div>`;
    }
    if (!t) return htl.html`<div data-feedback="filing" style=${muted}>${iss}…</div>`;
    const p = feedbackProgress(t), w = feedbackParse(t.issue.body);
    return htl.html`<div data-feedback=${p.closed ? "done" : "open"} style=${"border-left:3px solid " + (p.closed ? "#2a9d4b" : "var(--theme-foreground-faint)") + ";padding-left:8px"}>
      <div><b>${p.closed ? "Done" : p.state}</b> <code>${iss}</code></div>
      <div style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(w ? w.text : t.issue.title, limits.shown)}</div>
      ${p.links.length ? htl.html`<div style=${muted}>${p.links.join("; ")}</div>` : ""}
      ${p.closed && p.reason ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-reason style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(p.reason, limits.shown)}</div>` : p.last ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-last style=${muted + ";white-space:pre-wrap"}>${p.last.who}, ${new Date(p.last.at).toLocaleString()}: ${cut(p.last.text, limits.shown)}</div>` : ""}
      ${p.closed ? htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => remove(id)}>Remove</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || ""}</span></div>` : ""}
    </div>`;
  };
  const draw = (id) => els.get(id) && els.get(id).replaceChildren(view(id));
  const file = async (id) => {
    const text = String(drafts.get(id) || "").trim(), rec = store.get(id);
    if (!text || !rec) return (says.set(id, text ? "The note is gone." : "Write something first."), draw(id));
    const iss = "fb-" + id.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9-]/g, "").slice(0, 36);
    of.set(id, iss);
    filing.add(iss);
    draw(id);
    try {
      await client.procedure("issue.open", { key: "annotation/" + id, id: iss, title: cut(text.split("\n")[0], limits.title), body: feedbackBody(text, { anchor: rec.anchor, box: rec.box }, near(rec)), kind: "feedback", about: about(rec.anchor), labels: [limits.label] });
      await get(iss);
      drafts.delete(id);
      says.delete(id);
      store.patch(id, { issue: iss });
    } catch (e) {
      of.delete(id);
      says.set(id, "issue.open was refused: " + e.message);
    }
    filing.delete(iss);
    draw(id);
  };
  // Places a note for each labeled issue that has none here, and takes away a note whose issue lost the label.
  const sync = async () => {
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    try {
      const listed = (await client.query("issue.list", { label: limits.label, limit: 200 })).issues.filter((i) => !i.hidden);
      for (const i of listed) if (!tickets.has(i.id) || tickets.get(i.id).issue.updated_at !== i.updated_at) await get(i.id);
      const placed = new Set(of.values()), ids = new Set(listed.map((i) => i.id));
      for (const i of listed) {
        const where = !placed.has(i.id) && !hidden.has(i.id) && feedbackParse(tickets.get(i.id).issue.body);
        if (!where) continue;
        const a = store.create(where.anchor, { kind: limits.kind, issue: i.id, ...(where.box ? { box: where.box } : {}) });
        if (a) of.set(a.id, i.id);
      }
      for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
        if (ids.has(iss) || filing.has(iss)) continue;
        const t = await get(iss).catch(() => null);
        if (t && (t.issue.labels || []).includes(limits.label)) continue;
        of.delete(id);
        tickets.delete(iss);
        els.delete(id);
        store.remove(id);
      }
      for (const id of els.keys()) draw(id);
    } finally {
      busy = false;
    }
  };
  // Run when the page's notes change. A filed note that is no longer a cell was removed by the reader: when its
  // issue is closed the label comes off, and no page loads it again.
  const gone = async () => {
    for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
      if (await has(id)) continue;
      of.delete(id);
      els.delete(id);
      const t = tickets.get(iss);
      if (!t) continue;
      if (!t.issue.closed) hidden.add(iss);
      else {
        tickets.delete(iss);
        await client.procedure("issue.label", { key: `annotation/${iss}/removed`, id: iss, remove: [limits.label] }).catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: issue.label was refused: " + e.message));
      }
    }
    for (const id of [...drafts.keys()]) if (!of.has(id) && !(await has(id))) (drafts.delete(id), els.delete(id));
  };
  const remove = async (id) => {
    store.remove(id);
    await gone();
  };
  const note = (id) => {
    const el = htl.html`<div data-feedback-note=${id} style="font:13px var(--sans-serif)"></div>`;
    els.set(id, el);
    draw(id);
    return el;
  };
  const kind = { id: limits.kind, label: "Feedback", chip: "feedback", icon: "✉", order: 1, home: limits.home, box: { w: 280 }, note: ({ id }) => `feedbackNote(${JSON.stringify(id)})` };
  return { note, file, sync, gone, remove, kind, tickets, of, hidden, drafts };
}
// %%
// The text under a note's tip: the first element there that is in a cell and not in annotate's own layer.
feedbackNear = (rec, { resolve = a2Anchors.resolve, doc = document } = {}) => {
  try {
    const at = resolve(rec.anchor), p = at && (at.kind === "rects" ? at.rects[0] && { x: at.rects[0].left + 2, y: at.rects[0].top + 2 } : at);
    const el = p && doc.elementsFromPoint(p.x, p.y).find((e) => e.closest(".observablehq") && !e.closest("[data-a2-layer],[data-a2-root]"));
    return el ? el.textContent || "" : "";
  } catch {
    return "";
  }
}
// %%
feedback = feedbackOn ? feedbackApp({ client: brainClient, store: a2Store, near: feedbackNear, about: (anchor) => ((m) => (m ? m.worker : "brain"))(((brainModules && brainModules.modules) || []).find((m) => m.module === (anchor || {}).module)) }) : null
// %%
// The cell a note is: annotate writes `feedbackNote("<id>")` into this module for the kind below.
feedbackNote = (id) => (feedback ? feedback.note(id) : htl.html`<i>Feedback notes are for the owner, signed in at the Brain's address.</i>`)
// %%
feedbackKind = {
  if (!feedback) return "off: " + (!brainOrigin ? "not a Brain's address" : brainPortal ? "a portal" : !(brainWho && brainWho.owner) ? "the owner is not signed in" : "a verify page");
  plugins.add("annotate-kinds", feedback.kind, { invalidation });
  return "registered the kind feedback";
}
// %%
feedbackSync = {
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  // A note placed before annotate knows the kind would be written into the module it points at.
  feedbackKind;
  for (let i = 0; i < 400 && !a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 25));
  if (!a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind)) return "annotate has no kind " + feedbackLimits.kind;
  const tick = () => document.visibilityState === "visible" && feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  const timer = setInterval(tick, feedbackLimits.everyMs);
  invalidation.then(() => clearInterval(timer));
  await feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  return `asked at ${new Date().toISOString()}; ${feedback.of.size} notes`;
}
// %%
feedbackGone = {
  annotations;
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  await feedback.gone();
  return feedback.of.size;
}
// %%
// A tracker and annotate's store, in memory, for the tests.
feedbackRig = () => {
  const issues = new Map(), calls = [], cells = new Map();
  let n = 0, at = 1000;
  const client = {
    query: async (method, q = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, q]);
      if (method === "issue.list") return { issues: [...issues.values()].filter((t) => t.issue.labels.includes(q.label)).map((t) => ({ ...t.issue, body: undefined })) };
      if (method === "issue.get") return issues.has(q.id) ? structuredClone(issues.get(q.id)) : Promise.reject(new Error("no such issue"));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    },
    procedure: async (method, b = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, b]);
      if (method === "issue.open") {
        if (client.refuse) throw new Error(client.refuse);
        return void issues.set(b.id, { issue: { id: b.id, title: b.title, body: b.body, kind: b.kind, about: b.about, labels: [...b.labels], state: "open", closed: false, links: [], parent: null, updated_at: ++at }, events: [{ type: "opened", at, by: { caller: "owner" } }], children: [] });
      }
      if (method === "issue.label") return void ((t) => ((t.issue.labels = t.issue.labels.filter((l) => !b.remove.includes(l))), (t.issue.updated_at = ++at)))(issues.get(b.id));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    }
  };
  // What the loop does to an issue between two reads.
  const say = (id, event, change = {}) => ((t) => (t.events.push({ at: ++at, by: { caller: "token", holder: "secret:issues-implementer-2" }, ...event }), Object.assign(t.issue, change, { updated_at: at })))(issues.get(id));
  const store = {
    all: () => [...cells.values()],
    get: (id) => cells.get(id) || null,
    create: (anchor, fields = {}) => ((a) => (cells.set(a.id, a), a))({ id: "a2t" + ++n, anchor, box: { dx: 120, dy: -80, w: 240 }, ...fields }),
    patch: (id, fields) => void (cells.has(id) && cells.set(id, { ...cells.get(id), ...fields })),
    remove: (id) => void cells.delete(id),
    refresh: async () => {}
  };
  return { client, store, issues, calls, cells, say, app: () => feedbackApp({ client, store, near: () => "  Services\n table ", about: (a) => (a.module === "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues" ? "brain-x-issues" : "brain") }) };
}
// %%
test_feedback_body_keeps_the_anchor_and_says_where = {
  const anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues", cell: "issuesView", pid: "_p1", surface: "text", quote: { prefix: "For ", exact: "your attention", suffix: "" } };
  const body = feedbackBody("  The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.  ", { anchor, box: { dx: 1, dy: 2, w: 280 } });
  expect(body.startsWith("The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.\n\nAnnotated on the Brain's page: module `@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues`, cell `issuesView`, at the text \"your attention\".\n\n")).toBe(true);
  expect(feedbackParse(body)).toEqual({ text: "The count is wrong.\nIt says 3.", anchor, box: { dx: 1, dy: 2, w: 280 } });
  // Text that has a fence of its own, and a body nobody wrote this way.
  const fence = "`".repeat(3);
  expect(feedbackParse(feedbackBody(`see ${fence}annotation\n{"anchor":1}\n${fence}`, { anchor: { cell: "x" } })).anchor).toEqual({ cell: "x" });
  expect([feedbackParse("plain"), feedbackParse(`${fence}annotation\nnot json\n${fence}`), feedbackParse(`${fence}annotation\n{"box":{}}\n${fence}`), feedbackParse(undefined)]).toEqual([null, null, null, null]);
  expect([feedbackWhere({}), feedbackWhere({ quote: { exact: "foo" } }), feedbackWhere({}, " Services\n table ")]).toEqual(["Annotated on the Brain's page: no cell.", "Annotated on the Brain's page: at the text \"foo\", no cell.", "Annotated on the Brain's page: on the element that reads \"Services table\", no cell."]);
  return "the text, the sentence and the anchor go into a body and come back; a body without an anchor is null";
}
// %%
test_feedback_file_opens_an_issue_and_the_note_shows_it = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), app = rig.app();
  const a = rig.store.create({ module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues", cell: "issuesView", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5 } }, { kind: "feedback" });
  const el = app.note(a.id), press = (name) => [...el.querySelectorAll("button")].find((b) => b.textContent === name).click();
  const until = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 100 && !f(); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10)); return !!f(); };
  expect(el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback).toBe("draft");
  // Nothing written: nothing is sent.
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.textContent.includes("Write something first."))).toBe(true);
  expect(rig.calls).toEqual([]);
  const type = (text) => ((box) => ((box.value = text), box.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true }))))(el.querySelector("textarea"));
  // A refusal is said in the note, the text is kept, and the note is still a draft.
  rig.client.refuse = "not now";
  type("The table is too wide\non a phone.");
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.textContent.includes("issue.open was refused: not now"))).toBe(true);
  expect([el.querySelector("textarea").value, app.of.size]).toEqual(["The table is too wide\non a phone.", 0]);
  rig.client.refuse = null;
  press("File");
  expect(await until(() => el.querySelector("[data-feedback=open]"))).toBe(true);
  const sent = rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.open").at(-1)[1];
  expect(sent).toMatchObject({ key: "annotation/a2t1", id: "fb-a2t1", title: "The table is too wide", kind: "feedback", about: "brain-x-issues", labels: ["annotation"] });
  expect(feedbackParse(sent.body)).toEqual({ text: "The table is too wide\non a phone.", anchor: a.anchor, box: a.box });
  expect(sent.body.includes("Annotated on the Brain's page: module `@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues`, cell `issuesView`, on the element that reads \"Services table\".")).toBe(true);
  expect([el.textContent.includes("open"), el.textContent.includes("fb-a2t1"), el.textContent.includes("on a phone."), rig.store.get(a.id).issue, !!el.querySelector("textarea")]).toEqual([true, true, true, "fb-a2t1", false]);
  // A second app on the same page (the cell ran again) takes the filed note as its own and places no second one.
  const again = rig.app();
  await again.sync();
  expect([again.of.get(a.id), rig.cells.size]).toEqual(["fb-a2t1", 1]);
  return "an empty note sends nothing; a refusal keeps the text; File sends issue.open with the anchor and the note shows the issue";
}
// %%
test_feedback_load_places_a_note_for_each_labeled_issue = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-one", title: "One", body: feedbackBody("One", { anchor, box: { dx: 5, dy: 6, w: 300 } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "by-hand", title: "Labeled by hand", body: "no anchor", kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "other", title: "Not a note", body: feedbackBody("x", { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all()).toEqual([{ id: "a2t1", anchor, kind: "feedback", issue: "fb-one", box: { dx: 5, dy: 6, w: 300 } }]);
  // A second ask reads nothing again and places nothing again.
  const before = rig.calls.length;
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.calls.slice(before).map((c) => c[0]), rig.cells.size]).toEqual([["issue.list"], 1]);
  // Progress: a comment by the loop is read on the next ask, and drawn.
  const el = app.note("a2t1");
  rig.say("fb-one", { type: "commented", body: "Looking at the Services table now." });
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.calls.slice(-1)[0], el.querySelector("[data-feedback-last]").textContent.startsWith("implementer-2, "), el.textContent.includes("Looking at the Services table now.")]).toEqual([["issue.get", { id: "fb-one" }], true, true]);
  rig.say("fb-one", { type: "linked", rel: "cause", to: "services-table-width" }, { links: [{ rel: "cause", to: "services-table-width" }] });
  await app.sync();
  expect(el.textContent.includes("cause services-table-width")).toBe(true);
  // The label taken off elsewhere: the note leaves this page too, with no call of its own.
  rig.issues.get("fb-one").issue.labels = [];
  const calls = rig.calls.length;
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.cells.size, app.of.size, rig.calls.slice(calls).map((c) => c[0])]).toEqual([0, 0, ["issue.list", "issue.get"]]);
  return "one note for the issue with the label and an anchor; none for a body without one; progress is read when updated_at moves";
}
// %%
test_feedback_done_then_remove_takes_the_label_off = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), anchor = { cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.1, fy: 0.2 } };
  for (const id of ["fb-done", "fb-open"]) await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id, title: id, body: feedbackBody(id, { anchor }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  const idOf = (iss) => [...app.of].find(([, i]) => i === iss)[0], el = app.note(idOf("fb-done"));
  expect(el.querySelector("button")).toBe(null);
  rig.say("fb-done", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "The table scrolls sideways now: brain-x-page 1a2b3c." }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
  await app.sync();
  expect([el.querySelector("[data-feedback]").dataset.feedback, el.querySelector("b").textContent, el.querySelector("[data-feedback-reason]").textContent]).toEqual(["done", "Done", "The table scrolls sideways now: brain-x-page 1a2b3c."]);
  // Remove: the cell goes, the label goes, and the next ask places nothing.
  el.querySelector("button").click();
  for (let i = 0; i < 100 && rig.issues.get("fb-done").issue.labels.length; i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 10));
  expect(rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label")).toEqual([["issue.label", { key: "annotation/fb-done/removed", id: "fb-done", remove: ["annotation"] }]]);
  await app.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all().map((a) => a.issue)).toEqual(["fb-open"]);
  // The note of an open issue closed with annotate's own x: no call, hidden here, and back on the next load.
  rig.store.remove(idOf("fb-open"));
  await app.gone();
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length, rig.cells.size, [...app.hidden]]).toEqual([1, 0, ["fb-open"]]);
  const reloaded = rig.app();
  await reloaded.sync();
  expect(rig.store.all().map((a) => a.issue)).toEqual(["fb-open"]);
  return "a closed issue reads Done with its reason; Remove takes the label off once; an open one comes back on the next load";
}
// %%
// With annotate's own store, under a kind of the test's own: this page may have no kind feedback registered.
test_feedback_cells_stay_in_this_module_with_annotates_store = {
  const rig = feedbackRig(), limits = { ...feedbackLimits, kind: "feedbacktest" }, app = feedbackApp({ client: rig.client, store: a2Store, limits });
  const until = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 200 && !(await f()); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 25)); return !!(await f()); };
  const off = plugins.add("annotate-kinds", { ...app.kind, note: () => "1 + 1" });
  const mine = () => a2Store.all().filter((a) => a.kind === limits.kind);
  try {
    expect(await until(() => a2Store.kindOf(limits.kind))).toBe(true);
    const anchor = { module: "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", cell: "services", surface: "element", frac: { fx: 0.5, fy: 0.5 } };
    await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-real", title: "Real", body: feedbackBody("Real", { anchor, box: { dx: 7, dy: 8, w: 300 } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: ["annotation"] });
    await app.sync();
    expect(mine().map((a) => [a.issue, a.home, a.anchor.module, a.box])).toEqual([["fb-real", limits.home, "@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain", { dx: 7, dy: 8, w: 300 }]]);
    const id = mine()[0].id;
    // Moving the box writes the record again; it stays in this module, and the issue stays on it.
    a2Store.patch(id, { box: { dx: 9, dy: 9, w: 300 } });
    await a2Store.refresh();
    expect(mine().map((a) => [a.issue, a.home, a.box.dx])).toEqual([["fb-real", limits.home, 9]]);
    // A second app (the cell ran again) finds the note by what the record keeps.
    const again = feedbackApp({ client: rig.client, store: a2Store, limits });
    await again.sync();
    expect([again.of.get(id), mine().length]).toEqual(["fb-real", 1]);
    // Closed, then removed with the store's own remove (the box's x): the label comes off.
    rig.say("fb-real", { type: "moved", from: "open", to: "closed", reason: "done" }, { state: "closed", closed: true });
    await app.sync();
    a2Store.remove(id);
    await app.gone();
    expect([mine().length, rig.issues.get("fb-real").issue.labels, rig.calls.filter((c) => c[0] === "issue.label").length]).toEqual([0, [], 1]);
    return "placed in " + limits.home + " for a note about another module; kept there after a move; removed with the label";
  } finally {
    for (const a of mine()) a2Store.remove(a.id);
    off();
  }
}
// %%
test_feedback_near_reads_under_the_anchor_and_a_kept_note_without_its_label_goes = {
  // The anchor is what is resolved, not the record, whose cell is the note itself.
  const asked = [], el = { closest: (s) => s === ".observablehq", textContent: "Services" }, layer = { closest: () => true, textContent: "the note" };
  const doc = { elementsFromPoint: (x, y) => (asked.push([x, y]), [layer, el]) };
  expect([feedbackNear({ cell: "annotation_x_note", anchor: { cell: "services" } }, { resolve: (a) => (asked.push(a), { kind: "point", x: 3, y: 4 }), doc }), asked]).toEqual(["Services", [{ cell: "services" }, [3, 4]]]);
  expect(feedbackNear({ anchor: {} }, { resolve: () => ({ kind: "rects", rects: [{ left: 10, top: 20 }] }), doc })).toBe("Services");
  expect(feedbackNear({ anchor: {} }, { resolve: () => { throw new Error("gone"); }, doc })).toBe("");
  // A note kept from before, whose issue lost the label while no page was open: read once, then taken away.
  const rig = feedbackRig();
  await rig.client.procedure("issue.open", { id: "fb-old", title: "Old", body: feedbackBody("Old", { anchor: { cell: "x" } }), kind: "feedback", about: "brain", labels: [] });
  const a = rig.store.create({ cell: "x" }, { kind: "feedback", issue: "fb-old" });
  const app = rig.app();
  await app.sync();
  expect([rig.cells.size, app.of.size, rig.calls.slice(1).map((c) => c[0])]).toEqual([0, 0, ["issue.list", "issue.get"]]);
  return "near resolves the anchor; a kept note of an issue with no label is removed on the first ask";
}
// %%
test_feedback_is_off_away_from_the_owners_page = {
  expect(feedbackOn).toBe(!!brainOrigin && !brainPortal && !!(brainWho && brainWho.owner) && !/[#&]verify=/.test(location.hash));
  if (feedbackOn) return "on: this is the Brain's address with the owner signed in";
  expect([feedback, feedbackSync, feedbackNote("x").textContent]).toEqual([null, "off", "Feedback notes are for the owner, signed in at the Brain's address."]);
  expect(feedbackKind.startsWith("off: ")).toBe(true);
  return "off here (" + feedbackKind.slice(5) + "): no kind registered, no call made";
}
